  "_provenance": "STARTER PROFILE — generic, not derived from anyone's history. Copy to interests.json and edit, or better, run history_profile.py against your own browser and merge the proposal it writes. A profile built from what you actually read beats a hand-written one every time.",
  "_how_scoring_works": "An item's score = sum over matching topics of (weight x keyword-density bonus) x source trust x recency decay. An item matching NO topic is dropped, which is what keeps random noise out. Anything matching a global mute term is dropped outright. A topic may also declare require_any: at least one of those must match before the topic fires at all. It exists for include lists holding words that are only domain-specific in context — 'agent', 'benchmark' and 'evaluation' are LLM terms in an LLM article and ordinary English in a biology paper. Topics without require_any are unaffected.",
  "weights_guide": "3.0 = core, read every day. 2.0 = strong. 1.0 = adjacent, only if the item is excellent. 0 or enabled:false = off.",
